  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Support to Displaced Communities in North Kordofan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fighting between the SRF (Sudan Revolutionary Front) and the SAF (Sudan Armed Forces) in North and South Kordofan in late April has led to sudden, large scale displacement of families into North Kordofan.  
 
It is estimated that 20,000 people from Abu Kershola (pre-crisis population of 45,707) have been displaced to El Rahad town in North Kordofan.  About 15,000 of these have been provided with temporary shelter in four schools while others have been hosted by local families.  HAC (Sudan Humanitarian Aid Commission) reports that local authorities expect more displaced families to arrive in the coming days.  
 
The project aims to meet the food needs of 562 families displaced by the conflict. These families will be provided with a food basket each month for three months.  CAFOD will work with its strategic partner in North Kordofan, SIDO , with whom CAFOD is currently implementing an emergency education project. The project will be coordinated with the support of the Diocese of El Obeid.</narrative>
  </description>
